<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Villmergen Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1656, <a href="/years/1712">1712</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Villmergen Wars were two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-wars-of-religion">religious civil wars</a> of the Old Swiss Confederacy, both named after battles fought at Villmergen in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aargau">Aargau</a>. In the first, in 1656, the Catholic cantons defeated Zürich and Bern; in the second, in 1712, also called the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toggenburg-war">Toggenburg War</a>, the Reformed cantons won. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-aarau-1712">Peace of Aarau</a> of 1712 ended Catholic predominance in the Confederacy and gave Zürich and Bern control of the most important common lordships.</p></div>
